# LeetCode C++ Workspace

C++20 LeetCode problem workspace. Each problem lives in `problems/NNNN-slug/`. Full docs: `AGENTS.md`.

## Commands

```sh
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build -R NNNN --output-on-failure
./scripts/new.sh <number> <slug>
```

## New problem workflow

1. Scaffold → 2. `README.md` → 3. signature in `solution.hpp` → 4. tests first → 5. implement → 6. **`notes.md` required** → 7. paste to LeetCode

Read order for existing problems: README → notes → solution.

## Conventions

- `namespace lc::pNNNN` (zero-padded), `class Solution` in `solution.hpp`
- Header-only inline methods (one TU per test exe)
- `test.cpp`: `DOCTEST_CONFIG_IMPLEMENT_WITH_MAIN`, include `"solution.hpp"`
- Pair `make_list`/`make_tree` with `free_list`/`free_tree` or ASan leaks
- `std::size_t` for indices; `static_cast<int>` for LeetCode-shaped returns
- Strict warnings (`-Wconversion`): avoid `int` over `size()`

## Boundaries

- No CMake edits to add problems (glob auto-discovers)
- Keep `common/leetcode.hpp` flat; no inheritance or `ISolution` interface
- Do not switch doctest to `FetchContent_MakeAvailable` without CMake 4.x check
- Do not skip `notes.md` — it is the learning artifact

